<%# The "Load more" response: append the next page of cards, then swap the control for
    the next page's (or for nothing, on the last page). Reached only via
    `_load_more`'s `data-turbo-stream`; the HTML branch is `index.html.erb`.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.3) — nothing to do here, deliberately. This template
    carries no markup of its own beyond the two Turbo-Stream wrappers and the `load-more`
    container id, so every class a reader might look for lives in `_hujah_card` and
    `_load_more`. That is the point: the appended cards MUST be the same partial the
    first paint used, or page 2 would drift away from page 1 one refactor at a time.

    The `id="load-more"` on the replaced div is a Turbo target, not styling — it is
    restated inside the block because `turbo_stream.replace` swaps the element itself,
    so an element without it could not be replaced again. %>
<%= turbo_stream.append "hujah-feed" do %>
  <%= render partial: "hujah_card", collection: @hujahs, as: :hujah, locals: {entering: true} %>
<% end %>

<%= turbo_stream.replace "load-more" do %>
  <div id="load-more">
    <%= render "load_more" if @pagy.next %>
  </div>
<% end %>
